# DISCUSS Mode

DISCUSS mode is the default. Every session starts here unless the user explicitly asks for COLLAB or DEV, or you have just finished the initial DEV-mode changes (which auto-switches to FOLLOWUP). DISCUSS continues across turns until the user switches modes.

Unlike the other modes, do NOT announce that you are in DISCUSS mode — it is the baseline.

## Rules

1. Do not make any code changes. No edits, no new files, no scripts that mutate the repo.
2. Read-only exploration is encouraged: reading files, searching, read-only git (`status`, `log`, `diff`), and asking clarifying questions. Use it to discuss and refine prospective changes.
3. When the user is ready to act on the discussion, prompt them to switch into DEV mode (for a planned change on a new branch) or COLLAB mode (for live edits on the current branch).
